      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I write additional information.\n\nThese official and community-created worlds may contain artwork and other content that is copyrighted by someone other than the VRChat user.\n\nCurrently, users can place stickers anywhere on non-public worlds.\n\nThis means that users can break these artworks on non-public worlds.\n\nThis is an insult to the artists, and makes it difficult to publish such things as exhibition worlds on VRChat.\n\nRemember the incident of stupid people throwing tomato soup on the painting in the Louvre?\n\nThe same thing could happen on VRChat.\n\nIf it is possible to edit and update the world, there is a temporary solution such as changing the layers to Interactive, but this is a burden on the creators, and there is no solution if the world creator cannot upload for some reason. \n\nThere is no surefire solution for existing worlds, this is a big problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-26T22:32:36.546Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, only world authors can restrict sticker placement in public worlds.\n\nHowever, VRChat has many official and community-created worlds, and some non-public worlds (such as Friend+) should also have restrictions on sticker placement.\n\nI would like a system that allows the influence range to be applied to non-public worlds (such as Friend+).\n\nHere are some example worlds:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_fb95a2f0-180a-4729-bcc1-47a38e648056",
